# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
dist/
build/

# Node / dashboard
node_modules/
dashboard/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
dashboard/playwright-report/
dashboard/test-results/

# Environment & secrets
.env
deploy/.env
# Any deploy env file holds live credentials; only the templates ship.
deploy/.env.*
!deploy/.env.example
!deploy/.env.production.example
# Database dumps and blob archives from scripts/prod/backup.sh
backups/

# Trazo runtime artifacts (SDK spool/cache, local blob store)
.trazo/
blobs/

# Chaos corpus working directory (spool/cache per generated run) — only
# benchmark/corpus/failure_index.json (run refs) is committed, never the
# run payloads themselves (TRZ-P5-02).
benchmark/corpus/_runs/
# archive_run.py's local archive index: which runs this machine happens to
# have archived. Machine-local bookkeeping, not a shared artifact — unlike
# failure_index.json, which is the corpus definition and is committed.
benchmark/corpus/index.json

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Internal planning/design docs: kept locally, not published in the repo.
# README.md (any depth) and the root SECURITY.md are the exceptions --
# GitHub's own Security-tab vulnerability-reporting feature needs the
# latter actually published to work at all (SECURITY.md's own content
# tells readers to use it; TRZ-P7-05 caught this being silently untrue).
# The two benchmark results tables are also exceptions: unlike
# MASTER_PLAN.md/ROADMAP.md/etc., these aren't planning docs -- they're
# the actual P7 deliverable IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md §2 calls out
# ("Benchmark tables regenerate from scripts"), machine-regenerated by
# benchmark/detection/runner.py and benchmark/fidelity/run_harness.py.
*.md
!README.md
!/SECURITY.md
!benchmark/detection/results.md
!benchmark/fidelity/results.md

# Resumable scoring cache for the optional drift judge (one file per model)
benchmark/detection/.drift-cache-*.json
